cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  hybrid-hypoplastic-sand: a hybrid hypoplastic model for sands with fabric
  evolution, semifluidized state and coupled strain memory (MATLAB)
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jorge
    family-names: Rozas
    affiliation: Universidad Católica de la Santísima Concepción
repository-code: https://github.com/kokerozas/hybrid-hypoplastic-sand
abstract: >-
  MATLAB implementation of a hybrid hypoplastic constitutive model for sands
  under monotonic and cyclic loading: hypoplasticity of von Wolffersdorff
  (1996), intergranular strain of Niemunis and Herle (1997), fabric evolution
  and semifluidized state after Liao et al. (2022), and coupled cyclic and
  monotonic strain memories. Element-test driver, the calibrated parameter sets
  of Karlsruhe fine sand and Bio-Bio sand, and a script that reproduces the main
  results of the accompanying MSc thesis.
# MIT covers the work of J. Rozas P.; the original portions of the driver and data/KFS: NOTICE.md
license: MIT
version: "2026.10"
keywords:
  - hypoplasticity
  - constitutive modelling
  - liquefaction
  - cyclic mobility
  - intergranular strain
  - fabric tensor
  - semifluidized state
  - sand
  - Karlsruhe fine sand
  - Bio-Bio sand
